 2027. Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2. Both plans are mostly substations and transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (docs `utility-tenders`, `utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites (`datacentre-demand`). The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months (`grid-queue`). So data-centre demand is still growing, but at a slowing rate and capped by power supply.\n- **Order evidence:** VLTX utility order intake rose each quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$640M, C$655M and C$670M in 2026Q3 (`vltx_orders`). VLTX won 60% of the last tender round, so it is well placed to capture the new tenders.\n\nTwo caveats:\n- **Funding risk:** Utility funding is a risk to the capex plans. Another node (n3) found debt probably available but more expensive, and equity largely shut. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. A funding squeeze could delay or shrink the utility spending.\n- **Data gaps:** I did not find a figure for how much of VLTX's orders come from each buyer (the \"VLTX customer mix\"). I also did not find a 2026 comparison for the tender sizes. The C$900M and C$450M are the only dollar sizes I found.","ttft_ms":2636,"type":"result","duration_ms":46159,"uuid":"dea337d3-e807-4409-bfd1-e0fb3746785b","ttft_stream_ms":1482,"time_to_request_ms":578,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":37,"system_prompt":41,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":17,"input_attachments":123,"input_hooks":20,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":102,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":54,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":50,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":8,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":60,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":14,"client_cre